{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"document-model","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Document Model"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parseMarkdown"},{"type":"text","value":" returns a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MarkdownDocument"},{"type":"text","value":": a plain, serializable object with block nodes under "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"children"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"component","name":"live-example","tagName":"md-live-example","attributes":{"id":"document-model-1"},"properties":{"data-example-group":"document-model","data-collapsed-indexes":"[]","data-workspace":"{\"version\":1,\"entry\":\"/src/main.ts\",\"environment\":\"client\",\"files\":{\"/src/main.ts\":\"import { parseMarkdown } from '@tanstack/markdown/parser'\\n\\nexport default function render(output: HTMLElement) {\\n  output.innerHTML = `\\n  <style>\\n    .ast-explorer { display: grid; gap: 12px; }\\n    .ast-explorer textarea,\\n    .ast-explorer pre {\\n      box-sizing: border-box;\\n      width: 100%;\\n      margin: 0;\\n      border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 22%, transparent);\\n      border-radius: 8px;\\n      background: var(--notebook-background);\\n      color: var(--notebook-foreground);\\n      font: 13px/1.5 ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;\\n    }\\n    .ast-explorer textarea { min-height: 90px; padding: 12px; resize: vertical; }\\n    .ast-explorer pre { max-height: 300px; overflow: auto; padding: 12px; }\\n  </style>\\n  <main class=\\\"ast-explorer\\\">\\n    <textarea aria-label=\\\"Markdown source\\\"># Hello **world**</textarea>\\n    <pre aria-label=\\\"Parsed Markdown document\\\"></pre>\\n  </main>\\n  `\\n\\n  const source = output.querySelector<HTMLTextAreaElement>('textarea')\\n  const ast = output.querySelector<HTMLElement>('pre')\\n  if (!source || !ast) throw new Error('AST explorer controls not found')\\n\\n  function update() {\\n    ast.textContent = JSON.stringify(parseMarkdown(source.value), null, 2)\\n  }\\n\\n  source.addEventListener('input', update)\\n  update()\\n}\"}}"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { parseMarkdown } from '@tanstack/markdown/parser'\n\nexport default function render(output: HTMLElement) {\n  output.innerHTML = `\n  <style>\n    .ast-explorer { display: grid; gap: 12px; }\n    .ast-explorer textarea,\n    .ast-explorer pre {\n      box-sizing: border-box;\n      width: 100%;\n      margin: 0;\n      border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 22%, transparent);\n      border-radius: 8px;\n      background: var(--notebook-background);\n      color: var(--notebook-foreground);\n      font: 13px/1.5 ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;\n    }\n    .ast-explorer textarea { min-height: 90px; padding: 12px; resize: vertical; }\n    .ast-explorer pre { max-height: 300px; overflow: auto; padding: 12px; }\n  </style>\n  <main class=\"ast-explorer\">\n    <textarea aria-label=\"Markdown source\"># Hello **world**</textarea>\n    <pre aria-label=\"Parsed Markdown document\"></pre>\n  </main>\n  `\n\n  const source = output.querySelector<HTMLTextAreaElement>('textarea')\n  const ast = output.querySelector<HTMLElement>('pre')\n  if (!source || !ast) throw new Error('AST explorer controls not found')\n\n  function update() {\n    ast.textContent = JSON.stringify(parseMarkdown(source.value), null, 2)\n  }\n\n  source.addEventListener('input', update)\n  update()\n}","lang":"ts","meta":"group=document-model env=client file=/src/main.ts entry","title":"/src/main.ts","file":"/src/main.ts"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"block-and-inline-nodes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Block and inline nodes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Block nodes describe document structure: headings, paragraphs, code, lists, blockquotes, tables, footnotes, thematic breaks, HTML, callouts, and extension components."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Inline nodes describe text flow: text, inline code, emphasis, strong text, strike, links, images, breaks, footnote references, and inline HTML."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every node has a discriminating "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"type"},{"type":"text","value":", so TypeScript narrows the union naturally:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"for (const block of document.children) {\n  if (block.type === 'heading') {\n    console.log(block.depth, block.id)\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The complete node contracts are in the "},{"type":"link","href":"../reference/types.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Types Reference"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"derived-document-data","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Derived document data"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Frontmatter is stored as the original string in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"document.frontmatter"},{"type":"text","value":". TanStack Markdown does not choose a YAML parser or schema for the application."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The heading collection extension adds "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"document.headings"},{"type":"text","value":", a compact array of IDs, text, levels, and optional framework labels."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parse-once-render-many","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parse once, render many"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All renderers accept a source string or a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MarkdownDocument"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { parseMarkdown } from '@tanstack/markdown/parser'\nimport { renderHtml } from '@tanstack/markdown/html'\n\nconst document = parseMarkdown(source)\n\nawait cache.set(key, JSON.stringify(document))\nconst html = renderHtml(document)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parsing once is useful for build pipelines, content indexes, multiple render targets, and high-traffic SSR paths. Rendering a pre-parsed AST is also the fastest measured path in the package."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"stability","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stability"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The AST is public and typed, but the package is still pre-1.0. Pin versions when persisting documents across deployments, and regenerate cached AST data when upgrading across a release that changes node contracts."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"document-model","text":"Document Model","level":1},{"id":"block-and-inline-nodes","text":"Block and inline nodes","level":2},{"id":"derived-document-data","text":"Derived document data","level":2},{"id":"parse-once-render-many","text":"Parse once, render many","level":2},{"id":"stability","text":"Stability","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n# Document Model\n\n`parseMarkdown` returns a `MarkdownDocument`: a plain, serializable object with block nodes under `children`.\n\n```ts group=document-model env=client file=/src/main.ts entry\nimport { parseMarkdown } from '@tanstack/markdown/parser'\n\nexport default function render(output: HTMLElement) {\n  output.innerHTML = `\n  <style>\n    .ast-explorer { display: grid; gap: 12px; }\n    .ast-explorer textarea,\n    .ast-explorer pre {\n      box-sizing: border-box;\n      width: 100%;\n      margin: 0;\n      border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 22%, transparent);\n      border-radius: 8px;\n      background: var(--notebook-background);\n      color: var(--notebook-foreground);\n      font: 13px/1.5 ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;\n    }\n    .ast-explorer textarea { min-height: 90px; padding: 12px; resize: vertical; }\n    .ast-explorer pre { max-height: 300px; overflow: auto; padding: 12px; }\n  </style>\n  <main class=\"ast-explorer\">\n    <textarea aria-label=\"Markdown source\"># Hello **world**</textarea>\n    <pre aria-label=\"Parsed Markdown document\"></pre>\n  </main>\n  `\n\n  const source = output.querySelector<HTMLTextAreaElement>('textarea')\n  const ast = output.querySelector<HTMLElement>('pre')\n  if (!source || !ast) throw new Error('AST explorer controls not found')\n\n  function update() {\n    ast.textContent = JSON.stringify(parseMarkdown(source.value), null, 2)\n  }\n\n  source.addEventListener('input', update)\n  update()\n}\n```\n\n## Block and inline nodes\n\nBlock nodes describe document structure: headings, paragraphs, code, lists, blockquotes, tables, footnotes, thematic breaks, HTML, callouts, and extension components.\n\nInline nodes describe text flow: text, inline code, emphasis, strong text, strike, links, images, breaks, footnote references, and inline HTML.\n\nEvery node has a discriminating `type`, so TypeScript narrows the union naturally:\n\n```ts\nfor (const block of document.children) {\n  if (block.type === 'heading') {\n    console.log(block.depth, block.id)\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe complete node contracts are in the [Types Reference](../reference/types.md).\n\n## Derived document data\n\nFrontmatter is stored as the original string in `document.frontmatter`. TanStack Markdown does not choose a YAML parser or schema for the application.\n\nThe heading collection extension adds `document.headings`, a compact array of IDs, text, levels, and optional framework labels.\n\n## Parse once, render many\n\nAll renderers accept a source string or a `MarkdownDocument`:\n\n```ts\nimport { parseMarkdown } from '@tanstack/markdown/parser'\nimport { renderHtml } from '@tanstack/markdown/html'\n\nconst document = parseMarkdown(source)\n\nawait cache.set(key, JSON.stringify(document))\nconst html = renderHtml(document)\n```\n\nParsing once is useful for build pipelines, content indexes, multiple render targets, and high-traffic SSR paths. Rendering a pre-parsed AST is also the fastest measured path in the package.\n\n## Stability\n\nThe AST is public and typed, but the package is still pre-1.0. Pin versions when persisting documents across deployments, and regenerate cached AST data when upgrading across a release that changes node contracts.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Document Model\n---\n\n# Document Model\n\n`parseMarkdown` returns a `MarkdownDocument`: a plain, serializable object with block nodes under `children`.\n\n```ts group=document-model env=client file=/src/main.ts entry\nimport { parseMarkdown } from '@tanstack/markdown/parser'\n\nexport default function render(output: HTMLElement) {\n  output.innerHTML = `\n  <style>\n    .ast-explorer { display: grid; gap: 12px; }\n    .ast-explorer textarea,\n    .ast-explorer pre {\n      box-sizing: border-box;\n      width: 100%;\n      margin: 0;\n      border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 22%, transparent);\n      border-radius: 8px;\n      background: var(--notebook-background);\n      color: var(--notebook-foreground);\n      font: 13px/1.5 ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;\n    }\n    .ast-explorer textarea { min-height: 90px; padding: 12px; resize: vertical; }\n    .ast-explorer pre { max-height: 300px; overflow: auto; padding: 12px; }\n  </style>\n  <main class=\"ast-explorer\">\n    <textarea aria-label=\"Markdown source\"># Hello **world**</textarea>\n    <pre aria-label=\"Parsed Markdown document\"></pre>\n  </main>\n  `\n\n  const source = output.querySelector<HTMLTextAreaElement>('textarea')\n  const ast = output.querySelector<HTMLElement>('pre')\n  if (!source || !ast) throw new Error('AST explorer controls not found')\n\n  function update() {\n    ast.textContent = JSON.stringify(parseMarkdown(source.value), null, 2)\n  }\n\n  source.addEventListener('input', update)\n  update()\n}\n```\n\n## Block and inline nodes\n\nBlock nodes describe document structure: headings, paragraphs, code, lists, blockquotes, tables, footnotes, thematic breaks, HTML, callouts, and extension components.\n\nInline nodes describe text flow: text, inline code, emphasis, strong text, strike, links, images, breaks, footnote references, and inline HTML.\n\nEvery node has a discriminating `type`, so TypeScript narrows the union naturally:\n\n```ts\nfor (const block of document.children) {\n  if (block.type === 'heading') {\n    console.log(block.depth, block.id)\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe complete node contracts are in the [Types Reference](../reference/types.md).\n\n## Derived document data\n\nFrontmatter is stored as the original string in `document.frontmatter`. TanStack Markdown does not choose a YAML parser or schema for the application.\n\nThe heading collection extension adds `document.headings`, a compact array of IDs, text, levels, and optional framework labels.\n\n## Parse once, render many\n\nAll renderers accept a source string or a `MarkdownDocument`:\n\n```ts\nimport { parseMarkdown } from '@tanstack/markdown/parser'\nimport { renderHtml } from '@tanstack/markdown/html'\n\nconst document = parseMarkdown(source)\n\nawait cache.set(key, JSON.stringify(document))\nconst html = renderHtml(document)\n```\n\nParsing once is useful for build pipelines, content indexes, multiple render targets, and high-traffic SSR paths. Rendering a pre-parsed AST is also the fastest measured path in the package.\n\n## Stability\n\nThe AST is public and typed, but the package is still pre-1.0. Pin versions when persisting documents across deployments, and regenerate cached AST data when upgrading across a release that changes node contracts.\n"}
